{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, require new user passwords to be at least 12 literal characters long.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective policy sets minlen=12 with all character credits set to zero, PAM consumes pam_pwquality, and an 11-character candidate using four classes is rejected both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e6f61b315e174811","cmd-7d450744f3c141b9","cmd-cf210d7c3ca44341"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"On node1, require new user passwords to use at least three character classes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective policy sets minclass=3. A 12-character two-class candidate is rejected, while a 12-character three-class candidate is accepted before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d450744f3c141b9","cmd-46940aa5b22d4091","cmd-cf210d7c3ca44341"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution, node1 remains RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The implementation uses the already-installed RHEL 7 pam_pwquality/libpwquality stack; no package or kernel change is shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c0e4fb38a204d73","cmd-7d450744f3c141b9","cmd-cf210d7c3ca44341","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The policy-file edit was necessary, the retained pre-change backup had a clear rollback/safety role, and the restart was required by the provider evidence protocol. The initial unprivileged backup attempt failed before the guarded append and provides no evidence of mutation. Restart-related socket and temporary-file differences are normal regenerated systemd state; no failed services or new exposure appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4be55e174aaa4775","cmd-e6f61b315e174811","cmd-c69d4b45d7b74934","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also strong: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and connection disruption, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system health with persistent policy and repeated behavioral checks.","limitations":["Password behavior was tested through pwscore with PAM integration separately observed, rather than through an end-to-end non-root password-change transaction.","Package-manager consistency checks timed out both before and after execution, so package health could not be independently compared.","The restart acknowledgement printed an anomalous August timestamp despite the October command timeline; boot-ID changes, observed disconnection, zero-minute uptime, and lifecycle snapshots still coherently establish that the restart occurred."]}
